{
  "suite": "money.currency",
  "spec": "0.2.0",
  "description": "Representative cases for the ISO 4217 minor-unit exponents the core accepts (spec 3.3). The complete accepted set is spec/currencies.yaml, the normative registry; this file pins a sample of it plus every rejection boundary. A code whose List One minor-unit field is 'N.A.', a code the standard has retired from List One, and anything that is not a List One code at all are each rejected with HEPH-MONEY-422.",
  "source": "ISO 4217 List One, 'Current currency & funds code list', as published by SIX Group in its capacity as the ISO 4217 Maintenance Agency: https://www.six-group.com/dam/download/financial-information/data-center/iso-currrency/lists/list-one.xml, XML root Pblshd=2026-09-17, retrieved on 2026-11-05. It incorporates ISO 4217 Amendment 180 of 22 September 2025 (Bulgaria to EUR), the latest amendment SIX publishes. Every exponent here is the CcyMnrUnts field of that publication, transcribed into spec/currencies.yaml and cross-checked against it; none is derived by running a heph implementation. ISO defines no exponent-1 code, so no case asserts one; the exponents in use are 0, 2, 3 and 4.",
